":"Albutrellis Ellisii- Greening Goat's-foot Fungus","uri":"577c92_1404704621884087bd947b46c8a0ad6c~mv2.jpg","description":"An unusual and uncommon mushroom. We don't go looking for it but we are happy to partake if we find it! Delicious when sliced thinly and sautéed slowly for 30 minutes or more. I have frozen these and dehydrated them. They are quite large.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz2","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"ypq-461"},"title":"Greening Goat's-foot Fungus","uri":"577c92_77a2b3098a0c406681bb6fa6df90597a~mv2.jpg","description":"After cleaning up, drying out for a bit to be sliced thinly and either frozen or dehydrated.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz3","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-285"},"title":"Oyster Mushrooms - Pleurotus ostreatus","uri":"577c92_5a86e03b32e5427c99cd0676ebb2eae4~mv2.jpg","description":"Pleurotus ostreatus ready for the dehydrator.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz5","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-284"},"title":"Shrimp Russula - Russula xerampelina","uri":"577c92_2ee2ccf804084e8a9387132bc940fbad~mv2.jpg","description":"Russula xerampelina - After a brief cleaning with water and a soft toothbrush.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz6","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-283"},"title":"Shrimp Russula - Russula xerampelina","uri":"577c92_f453d6e8696542d0889ad574ebe4ecd3~mv2.jpg","description":"Russula xerampelina - Slicing for a sauté","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz7","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-282"},"title":"Shrimp Russula - Russula xerampelina","uri":"577c92_be30045ba06743f9b4769fdaae9397bc~mv2.jpg","description":"Russula xerampelina - After a quick cleaning in the field with a mushroom knife and brush.","width":3024,"height":4032,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx0","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-281"},"title":"Giant funnel Mushrooms - Leucopaxillus giganteus","uri":"577c92_11c50d250dbd4025b0dbea290846cc18~mv2.jpg","description":"Leucopaxillus giganteus - After a brief cleaning with water and a soft toothbrush.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx07","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-280"},"title":"The haul after a day of foraging","uri":"577c92_d9b8a5d6311a42b2a746b708bb330108~mv2.jpg","description":"Getting ready to clean and preserve Bear's Head Tooth Fungus, Shaggy Manes, Honey Mushrooms, Chicken of the woods.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx04","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-279"},"title":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis","uri":"577c92_59d36e0be2b843ebb3d63a34753418c6~mv2.jpg","description":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis cut in half to begin the separating and cleaning process","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx03","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-278"},"title":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis","uri":"577c92_134b0d3ffba347fd94eb8a766ef12a88~mv2.jpg","description":"Broken down to begin the cleaning process - Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx01","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-277"},"title":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis","uri":"577c92_e045bc28e5104048b3887b2a3c048810~mv2.jpg","description":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis after separating into smaller pieces and cleaning with water and a soft toothbrush.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx02","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-276"},"title":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis","uri":"577c92_95505cc73cdf42dfa135be10387c96ea~mv2.jpg","description":"Cauliflower Mushroom - Sparassis , broken into very small pieces and ready for the dehydrator.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx08","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-329"},"title":"Chicken of the woods - Laetiporus","uri":"577c92_dddc2ea3626045cb9ef78f81c3152e1c~mv2.jpg","description":"Chicken of the woods - Laetiporus after cleaning with water and a soft toothbrush, sliced and ready to be individually frozen then freezer bagged.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zywz4","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-274"},"title":"Armillaria - Ringed Honey Mushrooms","uri":"577c92_6d9dc05e360e41e49fc68d2107b13e3e~mv2.jpg","description":"Armillaria - Ringed Honey Mushrooms separated and cleaned with water and a soft toothbrush. Note the peeled stems. These are ready for individual freezing then they will be freezer bagged for storage.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx12","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-273"},"title":"Bear's Head Tooth Fungus - Hericium","uri":"577c92_c6f2e32d7eaf4a9097d9fa2601976aaa~mv2.jpg","description":"Separated and cleaned with a toothbrush and water, they are then hand shredded and ready for freezing. They will be freezer bagged for storage.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx05","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-294"},"title":"Bleeding Milk Cap - Lactarius rubrilacteus","uri":"577c92_829fa868e32240fba2dacd127293aeb0~mv2.jpg","description":"Bleeding Milk Cap - Lactarius rubrilacteus is a delicious mushroom that bruises bright green then turns a normal mushroom tan color when cooked. I will sauté these then freeze together. When cooked before freezing they do not need to be cooked again before serving so they can be used immediately after thawing in the refrigerator.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx06","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-293"},"title":"Lyophyllum decastes, Fried Chicken Mushrooms","uri":"577c92_27fb2a79fb6746df8c1071d99febd701~mv2.jpg","description":"Fried Chicken Mushrooms - Lyophyllum decastes, separated from their clumps, cleaned with water and a soft toothbrush, cut into smaller pieces if some are large then placed on sheet pans lined with parchment paper to be frozen individually then later freezer bagged for storage.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx1","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-292"},"title":"Chanterelles - Cantharellus californicus","uri":"577c92_adc34f6db9dc4a3fa1eefa422aab0d89~mv2.jpg","description":"Cantharellus californicus - we usually find these California chanterelles in the Southern Oregon Cascades but sometimes we find White Chanterelles as well.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx11","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-291"},"title":"Cantharellus californicus - Golden Chanterelles","uri":"577c92_52d68761fe8e4f90a6e29ba414ad122d~mv2.jpg","description":"Wash with water and tap lightly with a soft toothbrush to clean just before you are ready to cook or preserve. These will pull apart like string cheese to make smaller pieces.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx18","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-290"},"title":"Cantharellus californicus","uri":"577c92_d548b74e0d0841369b8f00b7f50bf053~mv2.jpg","description":"Cantharellus californicus - Golden Chanterelle cleaned before pulling or slicing.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx13","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-289"},"title":"Cocorra - Amanita vernicoccora","uri":"577c92_b5e794b723b245c884d780bf55949e9e~mv2.jpg","description":"Amanita vernicoccora - Do not eat these unless you have an expert identification. That said, they are an excellent choice mushroom you can find in the Spring. These have been cleaned removing some of the identifying aspects of this mushroom. They don't look like this when you find them.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx14","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-288"},"title":"Cocorra - Amanita vernicoccora","uri":"577c92_69f019f1af8a44b6b697fb28dda799ce~mv2.jpg","description":"After cleaning and chopping into manageable pieces, I freeze these individually then put them in a freezer bag for storage so I can remove just as many as I want to use at the time.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx15","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-287"},"title":"Matsutake - Tricholoma magnivelare","uri":"577c92_e89591779e864d90bc295a5b082c366f~mv2.jpg","description":"Matsutake - Pine Mushroom These mushrooms are very dense beautiful and tasty mushrooms! Don't wash until ready for use. I wrap them in foil and freeze them raw if preserving. Scrub them using water with a soft toothbrush or scrape them with a sharp knife to clean just before preparing them for cooking.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx16","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-296"},"title":"Shaggy Manes - Coprinus comatus","uri":"577c92_12df647070734326a0132209f52df43f~mv2.jpg","description":"Shaggy Manes - Coprinus comatus are a quickly perishable fungi so I like to rinse them, slice or chop and sauté them as soon as I can. They will begin to turn black and melt into ink if they are not cooked soon after they are picked. After cooking they can be frozen and used later.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""},{"type":"Image","id":"dataItem-lec0zyx17","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"h4w-295"},"title":"Yellow Coral Mushrooms - Ramaria rasilispora","uri":"577c92_cfb842b816084050b7038c4acb62690f~mv2.jpg","description":"Yellow Coral Mushrooms - Ramaria rasilispora are separated into florets and rinsed while tapping lightly with a soft toothbrush to remove debris just before preparing for cooking, freezing or dehydrating.","width":4032,"height":3024,"alt":""}]},"pageId":"zp2pi","hasWixTpaOnPage":false,"tpaInnerRouteConfig":{},"appPublicData":{"2979":{},"5210":{}},"isFixedHeader":false,"siteScale":1},"imageZoom":{"wPhotoConfig":{"comp-lebpi1zu":"dataItem-lebpi1zz","comp-lebpi21x":"dataItem-lebpi21y","comp-lebpi221":"dataItem-lebpi223","comp-lebpi224":"dataItem-lebpi2241","comp-lebpi227":"dataItem-lebpi228"},"tpaGalleriesComps":{"comp-lec0g73s":"comp-lec0g73s"},"nativeGalleriesComps":{},"shouldChangeUrl":true,"imageZoomCompType":"ImageZoom","deviceType":"Desktop","popupA11yExperimentEnabled":false,"translations":{"closeLabel":"Close","nextLabel":"Next","previousLabel":"Previous","expandedLabel":"Expanded image"},"imageDataItemIdToCompId":{"dataItem-lebpi1zz":"comp-lebpi1zu","dataItem-lebpi21y":"comp-lebpi21x","dataItem-lebpi223":"comp-lebpi221","dataItem-lebpi2241":"comp-lebpi224","dataItem-lebpi228":"comp-lebpi227","dataItem-lec0zywz":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywy":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywz1":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywz2":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywz3":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywz5":"comp-lec0g73s","dataItem-lec0zywz6":"co